{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1551785-a-mormon-hunter-compact-or-conspiracy","id":1551785,"title":"A Mormon hunter compact or conspiracy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-20T09:27:01-07:00","id":1551785,"title":"A Mormon hunter compact or conspiracy","content":"I had a interesting idea for a hunter compact or conspiracy within the Mormon Church and I would like some help developing it and differentiating it from groups like The Long Night.<br /> <br /> My basic idea is a group that's been around since the days of Brigham Young and was founded as a way to protect the Mormon community from Supernaturals that would prey on it. Somehow through a century or two of different Prophets and Compact leaders their official policy is sending in specialized Mormon Missionaries to try and preach to certain supernaturals depending on threat level, then sending in the armed teams if it fails and they prove a danger, with a endowment they claim comes from the Nephites themselves.<br /> <br /> Any help would be appreciated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T14:29:50-07:00","id":1551792,"title":"","content":"If you want some inspiration, in the WoD there is the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nephite_Priesthood\" target=\"_blank\">Nephite Priesthood</a>, a sorcerous organization that also designated themselves as protectors of the church, though keep in mind that there's obviously some differences from how that organization is run compared to the actual LDS church. Generally speaking, it's unlikely that Nephi himself would come as an angel when Moroni is already regarded as an angel providing revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-02T10:55:37-07:00","id":1552003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1551785-a-mormon-hunter-compact-or-conspiracy#post1551785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a interesting idea for a hunter compact or conspiracy within the Mormon Church and I would like some help developing it and differentiating it from groups like The Long Night.<br /> <br /> My basic idea is a group that's been around since the days of Brigham Young and was founded as a way to protect the Mormon community from Supernaturals that would prey on it. Somehow through a century or two of different Prophets and Compact leaders their official policy is sending in specialized Mormon Missionaries to try and preach to certain supernaturals depending on threat level, then sending in the armed teams if it fails and they prove a danger, with a endowment they claim comes from the Nephites themselves.<br /> <br /> Any help would be appreciated</div> </div> </div> </div>Mormon Missionaries themselves are something of a poor choice for a continuous compact/conspiracy of the church, given their two year time span, high mobility, and general youth. That said, proclaiming the gospel is a part of the threefold mission of the church, so even the non-tagged members have that sort of missive. The other two parts, perfecting the saints and redeeming the dead, are interesting to consider in the context of Chronicles and serve as decent foundations for the factions of the hunter organization.<br /> <br /> Differentiating from the Long Night feels a little...unnessecary, because it's not like the Mormon faith doesn't tackle many of the religions and spiritual themes differently from how Adventists or Jehovah's Witnesses would, to compare to other restorationist faiths. It's tempting to say that they're motivated by how the supernatural contradicts their cosmology and are thus desperately seeking revelation on the matter, but in practice, they tackle like subjects in the real world the way their peers do. Admittedly, the church doesn't have the eschatological focus their peers do-they are not obsessed with the Second Coming like the faiths that inform the Long Night do, and in fact don't believe in the concept of the Rapture, but honestly that just shunts them over to operationally looking more like the Union and their contemporaries than the Long Night. I'd study such and think on long time before trying to nail what, exactly, separated the LDS Church from their peers before committing to anything.<br /> <br /> If the organization goes in a direction that has an endowment, the big thing for Mormons is covenants, binding promises to God that are committed to by way of rituals is designated spaces. My preferred idea from the Mormon side has been covenants that might've emerged from attempts of the Nephites to infiltrate the Gadianton Robbers, possibly the longest standing opposition of the Nephites and a generally evil cult, that could easily run up against the supernatural. From a non-believer standpoint, covenants born from false histories, deceptive revelations, and pretend authority certainly has a vibe, and answering the question of what, if anything, is benefitting from their practices could answer a lot of operational questions about said organization.<br /> <br /> EDIT: A few things of clarification.<br /> <br /> 1) For the record, I am a former member and self-proclaimed apostate of the Church of the Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints, so that's my angle.<br /> <br /> 2) One of the big questions to tackle is how enmeshed or divorced is this compact/conspiracy from the church. It's one thing if there's a shadow priesthood for the supernatural world, it's another if hunters are looking for answers the church isn't providing but the members are finding that seem to indicate a build up to the former.<br /> <br /> 3) It also probably pays to ask the question of what you're hoping to express or otherwise get out of an explictly Mormon hunter organization, the themes and motifs you want to explore and make singular compared to the Long Night/Union/etc. I get the idea you like the idea of their missionary work to monsters explictly, and there's fun to be had in regarding monsters to the Tribes of Israel model, but you probably want dig a little more into the whys of that if you really want to flesh out what this thing should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-02-2025, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}